From 12d75f6abfc717b8905191eb48b149c3c6a4a09d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Suresh, Prashanth" <prashanth.suresh@intel.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 13:21:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] vpl-gpu-rt: Add statically-rendered mfx_features.h for
 Android.mk build

A real build (9m31s in, 3060/41884 targets) failed with a fatal
"'mfx_features.h' file not found" compiling
_studio/shared/include/mfx_config.h.

mfx_config.h's #include "mfx_features.h" is new in intel-onevpl-26.2.3
(confirmed absent from the pre-upgrade tree). Upstream normally
produces this file via CMake's
configure_file(mfx_features.h.in -> mfx_features.h) in
builder/BuildOptions.cmake, substituting each #cmakedefine MFX_ENABLE_*
based on CMake option() defaults. The Android.mk build has no
CMake-equivalent templating step, so this is a statically-rendered
copy of what that configure_file call would produce for the project's
plain defaults.

Cross-validated every flag against what _studio/mfx_lib/Android.mk
actually compiles: every MFX_ENABLE_* left defined here has matching
source wired into Android.mk (VPP, MCTF, ASC, ENCTOOLS, all listed
decoders/encoders, the extensive AV1/HEVC HW encode file lists), and
every one left undefined (JPEG_SW_FALLBACK, CPLIB, AENC, MVC/SVC video
encode) has no corresponding source wired in and isn't set anywhere in
the CMake build either. mfx_features.h.in is the only CMake-templated
header in this tree, confirmed via a repo-wide search for other *.h.in
files, so no other instance of this issue is expected.

Tracked-On: NIACP3-1547
Signed-off-by: Suresh, Prashanth <prashanth.suresh@intel.com>
---
 _studio/shared/include/mfx_features.h | 58 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 58 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 _studio/shared/include/mfx_features.h

diff --git a/_studio/shared/include/mfx_features.h b/_studio/shared/include/mfx_features.h
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..2e6f9236
--- /dev/null
+++ b/_studio/shared/include/mfx_features.h
@@ -0,0 +1,58 @@
